; What Fedora's SELinux policy lacks for clamd as the image starts it, installed by build_files/base/08-hardening.sh.
; tests/vm/suites/38-clamd-sandbox.sh checks that clamd starts without a denial.

; clamd@scan.socket hands clamd its socket, and libsystemd's sd_listen_fds() (systemd 258 and later) then checks
; LISTEN_PIDFDID: it opens a pidfd of its own process and asks fstatfs() whether it lies on pidfs. antivirus_t may
; not read the attributes of that file system, so every start was a denial in the audit log (which the security
; watcher reports while SELINUX_DENIALS is on) and libsystemd skipped the check that the sockets are clamd's own.
; Reading a file system's attributes gives nothing else.
(allow antivirus_t pidfs_t (filesystem (getattr)))
